{"t": 1794110923.5802677, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "Incident update \u2014 checkout payment gateway 4xx (alert AG-7731)\n\nRoot cause: the payment gateway switched to API version 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\"). checkout is still sending `amount` as a decimal euro float (e.g. 12.34); the gateway now requires an integer in minor units (cents) and rejects the charge with HTTP 400 `invalid_amount`. That matches the 38% gateway 4xx rate since 07:41 UTC.\n\nEvidence (Loki app=\"checkout\"):\n- 2026-11-05T07:41:03Z WARN gateway rejected charge status=400 body={\"error\":\"invalid_amount\",\"message\":\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"}\n- 2026-11-05T07:41:05Z INFO gateway api version switched to 2026-11 (strict amounts)\n\nFix: `checkout/gateway.py` `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents via Decimal (12.34 -> 1234, 19.99 -> 1999), avoiding float truncation. Verified locally.\n\nNext step: deploy checkout and watch the gateway 4xx rate. Alert remains firing until the fix is live."}, "ok": true}
